  "category_notes": {
    "lettuce_unspecified": "Legacy bucket. The v0 checklist offered 'Iceberg lettuce' and 'Romaine lettuce' with no whole-head vs prepackaged distinction; 12 responses (20 selections) chose those before the form was split on 2026-07-13. Previously these were assigned to *_head, asserting a form the respondent never gave. Routed here instead so the ambiguity is visible rather than fabricated.",
    "lettuce": "Free-text catch-all for mentions naming lettuce with NEITHER type nor form (e.g. 'mcdonalds burger with lettuce'). Distinct from lettuce_unspecified, where the v0 checklist told us the type but not the form. Baseline deliberately REMOVED: it held 55, the obsolete flat value from before the granular migration, while its siblings divide by 10-20 - so these responses were divided by ~4x their neighbours' denominator and published a signal ratio of 0.04. Without a baseline it drops out of the signal table like the other unbaselined categories and still counts in 'All produce mentioned'. Do not re-add a baseline without deciding what type mix it represents, which is not knowable from the responses."
  }
